tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [[92mINFO[0m] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>Imagine you're a stand-up comedian doing a set on the absurdity of modern dating apps.<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>*taps mic*

So I downloaded a dating app the other day—yeah, I know, my therapist was thrilled. And I’m scrolling through, and it hits me: we’ve gamified romance more than Las Vegas has gamified financial ruin.

*leans on mic stand*

You ever notice how we treat potential partners like we’re ordering a burrito at 2 AM? “Hmm, too much sour cream, NEXT. Oh, this one’s got guacamole but lives 47 miles away—PASS.” Meanwhile my grandparents met because my grandpa’s tractor got stuck in a ditch and my grandma happened to own the only rope in the county. That was it! That was the algorithm! “Proximity + rope = eternity.” Now I need a PhD in astrology and a 47-question compatibility quiz about whether pineapple belongs on pizza.

*paces stage*

And the photos! Everyone’s either cliff-diving in Bali or holding a fish they murdered. There is NO in-between. It’s either “I am one with the ocean” or “I conquered the ocean and this is my trophy.” Meanwhile I’m just trying to find someone whose main hobby isn’t “traveling” but does understand that “Let’s get coffee” actually means “Let’s stage a low-stakes job interview where we both pretend we’re not judging each other’s dental work.”

*adjusts collar*

Oh, and the height thing! Apparently every guy on there is *mysteriously* six feet tall. Every. Single. One. I’m starting to think it’s a government program. Meanwhile I saw a guy list his height as “5’12”” and I was like, “Sir, that IS six feet, but I respect the commitment to emotional truth in advertising.”

*grins*

And don’t get me STARTED on the prompts. “My love language is quality time.” Great, Brenda, mine is “not having to decode your entire personality from three pictures and a quote from *The Office*.”

*steps back, shrugs*

But here’s the thing—we keep swiping. Why? Because hope is the most addictive drug on the market, and it’s free until you pay $29.99 a month to see who already rejected you.

*mic drop... picks it back up because those things are expensive*

I’m Kimi, you’ve been beautiful, tip your bartenders and your therapists!

*shuffles off stage*<|im_end|>
